#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mutation-verify the AI's facts (docs/plans/plan_hl2mp_ai.md §8.2).

Each arm breaks one subject -- the core's references, the core's names, the
lane's native diff, a rule of the core -- rebuilds the AI's test project,
runs the facts that hold that subject, and requires them to go RED. Then the
arm is restored and, after every arm, the same facts must be GREEN again.

  tools/ai-mutations                 every arm
  tools/ai-mutations no-abi decide   the arms named
  tools/ai-mutations --list          the arms

Snapshot with a copy, restore from it with a FRESH mtime (never
`git checkout --`, never a copy that keeps the old mtime: MSBuild would skip
the rebuild and the next run would re-execute the mutant). Each arm proves
the mutation landed (the file's hash changed) and that the rebuild happened
(the test assembly's hash changed), and restores in a `finally`.
"""
import hashlib
import re
import os
import subprocess
import sys

